A vulnerability has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/frappe:hr">Frappe HR up to 16.15.0</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. This vulnerability affects the function <code>get_expense_claims/get_shift_requests/get_attendance_requests</code> of the file <em>hrms/api/__init__.py</em> of the component <em>Permission Validation</em>. This manipulation of the argument <em>employee</em> causes incorrect authorization.

This vulnerability is registered as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-101006">CVE-2026-101006</a>. Remote exploitation of the attack is possible. Furthermore, an exploit is available.

The vendor replied: &quot;This issue has already been reported by another individual, and based on that, we have fixed it.&quot;
